DNS

Human-readable hostnames instead of numeric IP addresses

Fully-Qualified Domain Name (FQDN): A domain name that is under a top-level provider
    Examples: .com  .mil .edu  .org  .net

DNS Heirarchy:

Root                    -       Answers requests in root zone

Top-Level Domain        -       .com .net .uk .it. fr

Second-Level Domain     -       diontraining.com        second-level = diontraining     top-level = .com

Subdomain               -       www.diontraining.com, support.diontraining.com, mail.diontraining.com

Host                   -       Refers to a specific machine


URL - Uniform Resource Locator

https://www.diontraining.com makes it secure

Host File   -   text file that serves as first point of contact when a device is seeking out communication with other devices over the network

